# npm 11+ GATES install scripts, and Electron's postinstall is what downloads the binary —
# so a fresh clone on any machine could install the package and ship no window at all
# ("electron are missing errors", 2026-11-08). The approval lives in the REPO so it is true
# for every user and every machine that clones it, not only for whoever edited ~/.npmrc.
# The three that need it: Electron (the desktop runtime), node-pty (terminal panes),
# esbuild (the bundler's native binary). Nothing else is approved.
allow-scripts=electron,node-pty,esbuild
